Protocol references (nothing copied)
------------------------------------
The optional ESPHome voice-satellite client (spec 0004) implements the client side of the ESPHome native API.
Message numbers, field numbers, and the Noise framing are facts about a wire format, read from:

* esphome/aioesphomeapi, `aioesphomeapi/api.proto`, `api_options.proto` and `_frame_helper/noise.py`
  (commit 9d32b21582cf4ed7b0a6a4390d4a4df9ca37f4d2, 2026-11-09), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018 Otto Winter.
* esphome/esphome, `esphome/components/api/api.proto` (commit 46f532e2bdcc8a8cae9dae1e4930a7ecbf0fc283), the
  ESPHome License: the repository states that C/C++ sources (.c, .cpp, .h, .hpp, .tcc, .ino) are GPLv3 and
  "the python codebase and all other parts" are MIT.

No file or generated code from either repository is included. The message encoder and decoder are written
independently from the documented wire behaviour. If a `.proto` file is ever vendored, add its MIT notice here.

Wake-word runtime (crates/wake)
-------------------------------
The audio frontend in crates/wake/src/frontend.rs implements the algorithm of the TensorFlow Lite Micro
microfrontend (tensorflow/lite/experimental/microfrontend, Apache License 2.0, Copyright The TensorFlow Authors)
and of the kiss FFT in its 16-bit fixed-point configuration (BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2003-2010 Mark
Borgerding). It is written independently and checked against the reference output; no source file is copied.
The test models in crates/wake/tests/golden/models are the official microWakeWord v2 models from
esphome/micro-wake-word-models (Apache License 2.0, Open Home Foundation); their LICENSE and NOTICE are kept beside
them, with the provenance record in crates/wake/tests/golden/PROVENANCE.txt.
